LOCAL MODIFICATION: HRC240DS

Allow record length up to 255 bytes for UPDATE 

Affected Files:
===============

DMSUPD   ASSEMBLE
EXECUPDT EXEC     (new file)

Prerequisites:
==============

none

Description:
============

This update extends the UPDATE command to support source files with  
record lengths up to 255 bytes.  The updated file format rules are:

 -- The input source file must be fixed format with a record
    length between 80 and 255 bytes.
 -- All update files must be the same format as the input file
 -- The SID and sequence numbers are still in the last 17
    columns of the source/update files regardless of length.
 -- CNTRL and AUX files must still be fixed length with 
    80 byte records
 
 This update also makes a slight change to the update log file
 format when the input files are wider than 80 bytes. In this case,
 the log file will have a record size of 121 bytes.

Details:
========

DMSUPD ASSEMBLE
---------------

Most of the updates to this module were to support dynamic record
length handling. There are a couple of other notable changes:

 -- It was necessary to add an additional (4th!!) base register.
    R6 was chosen to fill this role.
    
 -- As mentioned in the description, the output update log now has
    a slightly different format when the source/update file records
    are longer than 80 bytes. These changes are:
    
    * The update log listing file will have a LRECL of 121
    * If the source/update records ae longer than 104 (120-16),
      then the log line will consist of the first 82 columns
      of the logged record (104-5-17) followed by an ellipse (' ... ')
      and the right most 17 columns of the record so the log  will 
      still show the SID and sequence

 -- Two new error messages are added:
 
    DMSUPD007E File 'fileid' does not have a logical record length >= 80 and <= 255
    DMSUPD007E File 'updfile' does not have the same format and record length as 'srcfile'
  
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

EXECUPDT EXEC (new file)
-------------

This new EXEC is a functionally equivalent subset of the EXECUPDT tool
that is part of later versions of VM.  Those versions of VM use this
tool to maintain REXX files using the UPDATE command.  

EXECUPDT can use UPDATE To maintain files that would normally have
variable length records without any sequence numbers.  The following
outlines the approach to take for a sample file:  GADGET EXEC

-- The base source file has fixed length records at least 17 bytes
   longer than the actual source statements and having sequence
   numbers in the last eight columns.
   
-- The base source file would be named:  GADGET $EXEC

-- EXECUPDT would be used to apply updates to this file and produce
   the update listing and log file.
   
-- The result of the EXECUPDT processing would be a file with variable
   length records having the last 17 columns and extra trailing space
   removed. The name of this result file would be:  GADGET EXEC
   This is the file that would be placed in the build target.

The EXECUPDT command syntax is:

   EXECUPDT fn <ft   <fm   >> <(options...<)>>
                EXEC  *
   Where:
 
   fn ft fm
         is the file identifier of the source input file.  The
         file must consist of card image records with length
         less than or equal to 255.  Record format must be
         Fixed.
         The last 8 columns of each card image must contain
         a sequence number.
         If the filetype or filemode are omitted,
         EXEC and * are assumed, respectively.
 
  Options:
 
     CTL cfn  specifies that "cfn CNTRL" is an update control
              file that controls the application of multiple
              update files to the source input file.
  
     NOUPdate specifies that no update files are to be
              applied to the source.  The HISTORY option
              will be ignored if this is specified.
 
     HISTory  specifies that the file 'cfn UPDATES' which is
              created by the UPDATE command is to be appended
              to the updated source as a comment.
 
     NOHISTory specifies that no history log is to be appended
              to the updated source.  This is the default.
 
     SID      specifies that the last 17 columns contain
              information to be removed from the source file.
              This must be in the format
 
                   n-16            n ( <= 255 )
                   |               |
                   V               V
                   SID_CODE SEQ_NUMB
 
     NOSID    specifies that only sequence numbers are to be
              removed from the updated source (the last 8
              columns).  This is the default.
 
     Other options as with the UPDATE command.

This version of EXECUPDT does not do any of the other file modification
steps that the REXX version in newer VM systems does like stripping
out comments or compacting the result file.

 One note: There is a school of thought that the EXEC control files that
 are used to build and maintain VM (e.g. CPLOAD EXEC) should be managed
 using UPDATE. Most of these files can be managed with UPDATE without
 needing this new EXECUPDT tool since old school EXEC files that have
 fixed length 80 byte records can also have sequence numbers since the
 old EXEC processor only uses columns 1-72 of fixed-80 records.
 
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

